| Monthly payment | $6,007 | $7,015 | **+$1,008/mo (+16.8%)** |
| TDSR | 30.0% | 35.1% | +5.1pp |
| TDSR breach (55% cap) | No | **No** | — |
| Gross buffer (vs $20K income) | $13,993/mo | $12,985/mo | -$1,008 |
| Est. net after living (~$4,500/mo) | ~$9,493 | ~$8,485 | -$1,008 |

### Verdict: SURVIVE

The 150bps shock adds $1,008/mo — meaningful but not a crisis. TDSR at 5.0% is 35.1% — still 19.9pp below the 55% cap. Rates would need to reach approximately 12.5% to trigger a TDSR breach.

